# Cache policy for the web deploy.
#
# WHY: a hashed-asset SPA must NEVER let index.html (or the SW/manifest) be cached for a fixed
# window. If a stale index.html is served after a deploy, it references asset hashes that were
# deleted by that deploy → those chunks 404 → the app can't boot → blank white page until the cache
# expires. So the entry documents are always revalidated (no-cache), while the content-addressed
# files under /assets/* (their hash changes when their content changes) are cached forever.
#
# This file is honored by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. On any other host (nginx, Vercel, a plain
# static server, a CDN) set the EQUIVALENT headers there — this file alone won't apply.
# Rule order matters: later matches override earlier ones for the same header, so /assets/* (below)
# wins over /* for the hashed assets.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
